{"id": "EUVD-2026-32433", "enisaUuid": "227042c2-28ba-3710-a214-3ff510a3ef6c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmd/raid5: fix soft lockup in retry_aligned_read()\n\nWhen retry_aligned_read() encounters an overlapped stripe, it releases\nthe stripe via raid5_release_stripe() which puts it on the lockless\nreleased_stripes llist. In the next raid5d loop iteration,\nrelease_stripe_list() drains the stripe onto handle_list (since\nSTRIPE_HANDLE is set by the original IO), but retry_aligned_read()\nruns before handle_active_stripes() and removes the stripe from\nhandle_list via find_get_stripe() -> list_del_init(). This prevents\nhandle_stripe() from ever processing the stripe to resolve the\noverlap, causing an infinite loop and soft lockup.\n\nFix this by using __release_stripe() with temp_inactive_list instead\nof raid5_release_stripe() in the failure path, so the stripe does not\ngo through the released_stripes llist. This allows raid5d to break out\nof its loop, and the overlap will be resolved when the stripe is\neventually processed by handle_stripe().", "datePublished": "2026-05-27T12:57:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T01:20:15", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/66df9f30673db66ac35145820a8e24906069ae57", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4166d5234fe8b6c3c7f796a6c198605356c5b355", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a9055300e07d9d6800264d3c2560e1d0144689ca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/09880592f5a9dc73377d6eb5ac123537b5f8df49", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/80fc6ca2cbde018d52e13f305edcd643911bd94b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1985cb3247e87ff6b8ca4bc5f9626f4f51024507", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/883cc33b7af1c448663287f069ef9dfea001e90f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7f9f7c697474268d9ef9479df3ddfe7cdcfbbffc"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mgf2-2rm5-mvrf", "CVE-2026-46051"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "163a2f83-b55f-3af5-b026-c46b47b084be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "773ca82fa1ee58dd1bf88b6a5ca385ec83a2cac6 <4166d5234fe8b6c3c7f796a6c198605356c5b355"}, {"id": "1829832b-9070-3eba-ae67-d35a4a1b2b86", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "773ca82fa1ee58dd1bf88b6a5ca385ec83a2cac6 <a9055300e07d9d6800264d3c2560e1d0144689ca"}, {"id": "336ee6a1-7c78-3f19-a446-489483ba3be6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.175"}, {"id": "408b3e33-c5a8-30d2-a499-979e45be5609", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.140"}, {"id": "43eb3dad-70c6-36aa-b640-1395a8af8de9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "773ca82fa1ee58dd1bf88b6a5ca385ec83a2cac6 <80fc6ca2cbde018d52e13f305edcd643911bd94b"}, {"id": "447e160d-2838-3909-bee4-e49b0e692c17", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "773ca82fa1ee58dd1bf88b6a5ca385ec83a2cac6 <7f9f7c697474268d9ef9479df3ddfe7cdcfbbffc"}, {"id": "4a4c637d-8aeb-3de7-8d0f-c40cf480c0bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.86"}, {"id": "56cfacb5-f5bd-3c7c-825f-32cbb9d42337", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.12"}, {"id": "5f9780c5-5580-39fc-8e4d-9af6f707e086", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.209"}, {"id": "790b8b24-a02c-3be6-a6ed-99f7e70cdbdc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "773ca82fa1ee58dd1bf88b6a5ca385ec83a2cac6 <66df9f30673db66ac35145820a8e24906069ae57"}, {"id": "7b82b8bd-5b02-3f63-88ee-ac423ddcc8ac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.258"}, {"id": "a67b5c5a-34ab-367c-9ca9-3f05b80042ac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "pat